---
source: crates/zeff-engine/tests/na_comparison.rs
expression: all
---
== in_where
error[Z0226]: `== NA` is never true: a comparison with `NA` gives `NA`, not true or false
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:18
  |
2 | s.where(score == NA)
  |                  ^^ the literal `NA`
  |
  = help: write `is_missing(score)`; `NA` stands for a value that is not known, so nothing is known to equal it

== in_where_not_equal
error[Z0226]: `!= NA` is never true: a comparison with `NA` gives `NA`, not true or false
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:18
  |
2 | s.where(score != NA).n_rows()
  |                  ^^ the literal `NA`
  |
  = help: write `!is_missing(score)`; `NA` stands for a value that is not known, so nothing is known to equal it

